abstract: >-
  Spacefield Transformation I formulates the minimal Spacefield
  Transformation (SFT) and Universal Confinement Zone (UCZ)
  cosmological closure framework. The dimensionless closure structure
  is distinguished from the specified dimensional confinement
  normalization of the minimal SFT branch. Conditional on this
  normalization, the framework determines baseline matter and
  confinement scales, while observationally anchored present-epoch
  cosmological quantities are used to reconstruct the corresponding
  late-time background. The paper also introduces a phenomenological
  dark-energy boundary-scaling law and studies conditional
  observational signatures relative to Lambda-CDM, including
  supernova, expansion-rate, and standard-siren distance residuals.

